# Rust build output. Unanchored: `crates/aemulator-hvf` and `aemulator-studio/src-tauri` are
# workspace-EXCLUDED (see the note in Cargo.toml), so each builds into its own `target/` rather
# than the workspace root's. Anchoring this to `/target` would leave those two committable.
target/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak

# Run logs. Nothing in this tree authors a `.log`; every one is emulator/build output.
*.log

# Test-workload APKs — fetched, not authored (3DMarkandroid is 335 MB). `.xapk` is the APKPure
# split-APK bundle (a zip of APKs), same provenance and same reason not to commit it.
*.apk
*.xapk

# Built / downloaded disk images and firmware (never commit multi-GB blobs)
*.img
*.img.*
*.dtb
*.qcow2
*.raw

# Oracle downloaded assets (Cuttlefish images, GSIs, kernels, build.prop dumps)
/oracle/assets/
/oracle/downloads/
/oracle/**/*.zip
/oracle/**/*.tar.*

# Out-of-tree build dependencies. third_party/bootstrap.sh clones gfxstream, aemu and mesa here at
# the SHAs third_party/MANIFEST.sh pins, then builds them in place (~1.2GB of source + build dirs +
# a python venv + install prefixes). Only the manifest, the resolver, the bootstrap and our patch
# series are tracked; everything else is reproducible from them.
#
# Ignore the DIRECTORY CONTENTS and re-admit the tracked files by name, rather than listing each
# checkout: git cannot un-ignore a file whose parent directory is ignored, so a new dep appearing
# under third_party/ must default to ignored — otherwise the first bootstrap on a fresh clone offers
# a vendored source tree for commit.
/third_party/*
!/third_party/MANIFEST.sh
!/third_party/paths.sh
!/third_party/bootstrap.sh
!/third_party/regen-cereal.sh
!/third_party/downgrade-registry.py
!/third_party/patches/

# Editor / OS cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
